+# Daily Grind styling
+
+`index.html` loads `styles.css` directly; no CSS build step or runtime is required.
+
+The layer order is `tokens → reset → base → layout → components → utilities`.
+Keep all author rules in a layer: unlayered rules outrank normal layered rules.
+Use the utility layer for intentional overrides instead of `!important` or longer
+selectors.
+
+Shared custom properties live in `:root`. Palette primitives feed semantic colors;
+spacing, typography, radii, motion, and layout values are named tokens. Keep values
+used by only one component (such as the hero image or button variants) local to
+that component. Change semantic tokens to restyle the site consistently.
+
+Reset and base selectors use `:where()` for zero specificity. Reset only the element
+types owned by the page, rather than every element with `*`. Components use class
+roots and shallow native nesting; direct-child selectors keep rules from matching
+unrelated nested components. Use `:where()` for child types and interaction states
+so these filters do not increase specificity. This site does not need `@scope`
+proximity rules: explicit component boundaries suffice without a scope fallback.
+
+Use logical spacing and sizing properties. Navigation wraps and the grid minimum
+shrinks to its available width on small screens. The hero uses minimum height so
+content can grow with text zoom. Preserve keyboard focus indicators and respect
+reduced-motion preferences when adding interactions.
